# ACF Integration

ACF Pro required. Use `get_field()` only — no `have_rows()` or `the_field()`.

## Options page

Global fields via `get_field('field_name', 'option')`:

```php
$phone = get_field('phone', 'option');
```

Registered in `functions.php` on `acf/init`.

## Shared home content (post ID 10)

FAQ, CTA, and Gallery sections load from a fixed post ID (environment-specific):

```php
$faq = get_field('faq', 10);
$cta = get_field('cta', 10);
$gallery = get_field('gallery', 10);
```

Update ID when front page changes on new installs.

## Section field groups

| Section | ACF group | Key fields |
|---------|-----------|------------|
| Hero | `hero` | image, sub_title, title, content |
| Purpose | `about` | image, image_bg, sub_title, title, content |
| Wood | `sub_banner` / `sub_banner_copy` | image, titles, content |
| Vibe | `good_times` | image, youtube_video, items repeater |
| Pizza | `pizza` | items repeater |

## Event CPT fields

- `event_date` — return format `Ymd` recommended
- `event_start_time`, `event_end_time` — time pickers
- Legacy: `event_time`, `event_end`

Queried via `hotw_whats_on_get_event_date_for_post()` in `inc/whats-on-events.php`.

## Output escaping

```php
echo esc_html($title);
echo esc_url($link);
echo wp_kses_post($content); // when HTML is intentional
```

## No acf-json sync yet

Field groups are configured in WP admin. Export to `acf-json/` when ready for version control.
